# Example EnvironmentFile for thoth-mesh-node.service - copy to
# /etc/thoth-mesh/node.env (root-owned, mode 0640 is enough since
# DynamicUser's ephemeral group gets read access) and edit.
#
# NODE_ARGS is word-split by systemd the same way a shell would, since
# ExecStart= references it unquoted ($NODE_ARGS, not ${NODE_ARGS}) -
# ordinary flags separated by spaces, same as on the command line.
# thoth-mesh-node's own --help documents every flag; see also
# docs/OPERATIONS.md.
#
# Every flag below can go in a TOML config file instead (see
# docs/OPERATIONS.md's "Node config file" section and ADR-0054) - set
# NODE_ARGS=--config /etc/thoth-mesh/node.toml here and put the actual
# settings there instead, if you'd rather not grow this one long line.

# 0.0.0.0, not the 127.0.0.1 default - a node bound to loopback can't
# be dialed by another node or a remote client.
NODE_ARGS=--addr 0.0.0.0:49500 --log-level info

# A more complete example, federating with two seed peers, serving
# metrics, and running with TLS:
#
# NODE_ARGS=--addr 0.0.0.0:49500 --log-level info \
#   --peer node-b.internal:49500 --peer node-c.internal:49500 \
#   --metrics-addr 0.0.0.0:9090 --metrics-token-file /etc/thoth-mesh/metrics-token \
#   --tls-cert /etc/thoth-mesh/node-cert.pem \
#   --tls-key /etc/thoth-mesh/node-key.pem \
#   --tls-ca /etc/thoth-mesh/ca-cert.pem
